        "member_id": "olsson-eva",
        "point": "Olsson prefers aberration-corrected electron optics, describing a mature instrument advance that changed what microscopy could resolve, while flagging priority among parallel efforts and individual attribution.",
        "response": "The transformation in imaging capability is compelling, and decades of use support the maturity of B057. The unresolved priority and attribution questions are substantial, however. B012 also needs historical scrutiny, but its proposed scope links a particular prediction to a specific experimental realization, giving the citation a more defined physical result."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "mehlig-bernhard",
        "point": "Mehlig prefers conformal field theory and exact results in two-dimensional critical phenomena, emphasizing its theoretical reach while acknowledging its broad boundary and the distinct contributions of the proposed laureates.",
